14:["$","p","b4738",{"children":["That distinction is missing from almost every roundup in this category, which sorts on template counts and price instead. It's also the only thing that matters when the output is going on a pitch deck, a print run or a product page, because a logo with a tapered stroke and a redrawn counter is not your logo."]}]
15:["$","h2","b4740",{"id":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What to know before you pick"]}]
16:["$","ul","b4742-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4742",{"children":["Work out which of the three mechanisms a tool uses before you look at anything else. Several vendors ship a library path and a generative path under one brand and one price, and only one of them preserves your file."]}],["$","li","b4744",{"children":["Generative models garble text as it gets longer. Ideogram's own prompting guide says short, punchy phrases work best, that the longer the text the higher the chance of spelling errors and distortions, and that long passages should be added afterward in a graphic editor. Fine for a logo lockup, useless for a packaging back panel."]}],["$","li","b4746",{"children":["A generated mockup is a flat file. There's no smart object underneath, so you can't swap tomorrow's design into yesterday's render without generating the whole thing again."]}],["$","li","b4748",{"children":["Check the commercial license tier, not just the price. On several tools here the free plan grants no commercial rights, and on one of them free-plan output is owned by the vendor and published publicly."]}],["$","li","b4750",{"children":["Screen-fine isn't print-fine. Soft edges and slight letterform distortion survive a slide and fall apart on embroidery, small sizes and merchandise."]}]]}]
17:["$","h2","b4752",{"id":"the-three-mechanisms-and-what-each-does-to-your-logo","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["The three mechanisms, and what each does to your logo"]}]
18:["$","p","b4754",{"children":["A template library pairs a pre-shot photograph with a fixed warp. Your file is mapped onto the surface by the template rather than redrawn, so the result is deterministic and repeatable, and the logo that comes back is exactly the one you supplied. The limit is that you can only use scenes someone already shot."]}]
19:["$","p","b4756",{"children":["True 3D rendering puts your artwork on an actual mesh as a texture or decal, then computes the lighting and distortion. Same fidelity guarantee, more freedom of angle, and it's the only route that handles packaging dielines properly. Adobe's Illustrator Mockup sits just off this category, using a neural network to infer the 3D shape of a single photograph and then mapping a vector decal onto it. Adobe says the feature preserves the quality of a decal as users place it on the 3D surface, and separately that vector decals keep a 3D preview working regardless of its resolution."]}]
1a:["$","p","b4758",{"children":["Generative placement asks a diffusion or autoregressive model to produce the whole image. Nothing is preserved, because nothing is placed; it's all drawn. A comparison published in April 2026 by Creatsy, a PSD mockup vendor, put seven generative models across six products and found that Midjourney's logo text on a kraft bag came back recognizable from a distance and unreadable up close, and that label text was a mess across the board on a cosmetic jar. The ranking carries an obvious interest, but the observations are specific and easy to reproduce."]}]
1b:["$","p","b4760",{"children":["The useful conclusion isn't that generative tools are bad at mockups. It's that a generative tool only preserves a mark if the workflow puts the mark back on top rather than asking the model to draw it."]}]
1c:["$","h2","b4762",{"id":"what-separates-a-good-brand-mockup-tool","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What separates a good brand mockup tool"]}]
1d:["$","p","b4764",{"children":["There are four criteria here, and the first two are the ones most roundups skip."]}]
1e:["$","h3","b4766",{"children":["Whether your artwork survives"]}]
1f:["$","p","b4768",{"children":["Ask where your file ends up in the pipeline. If it's a layer composited over the render, or a decal mapped onto geometry, it survives. If it's a description the model reads before drawing, it doesn't. Adobe documents this most fully and Dynamic Mockups states it plainly for its template path; most of the others don't say either way, so the mechanism is usually a better guide than the marketing copy."]}]
20:["$","h3","b4770",{"children":["Whether type stays legible"]}]
21:["$","p","b4772",{"children":["Typography is where generative mockups break most visibly, and the models differ sharply. GPT Image 2 is the model most often cited for multilingual in-image text, and OpenAI's launch material names Bengali, Chinese, Hindi, Japanese and Korean as the languages where it gained most. Ideogram 4.0 takes bounding boxes and hex colors as structured input, so you control the layout. Recraft outputs scalable vector graphics (SVG), which turns a wrong letterform into a path you reshape instead of a generation you redo. None of them handles a paragraph."]}]
22:["$","h3","b4774",{"children":["Whether it holds a brand system"]}]
23:["$","p","b4776",{"children":["One mockup is a demo. A brand needs the same palette, type and logo treatment across a deck, a storefront, a packaging render and a social placement. Look for something that pins those values once and applies them to everything afterward, and check where the pinning lives: an account-level brand kit follows you between projects, while a setup that lives inside one working file has to be carried over by hand each time."]}]
24:["$","h3","b4778",{"children":["What the license actually grants"]}]
25:["$","p","b4780",{"children":["Licensing here isn't consistent from tool to tool. Some free tiers grant no commercial rights at all; one vendor retains ownership of free-plan images and publishes them in a public gallery; one 3D tool restricts its lower tiers to personal use and grants commercial use and resale only at the top; another caps commercial reproduction at a fixed number of copies per design on its mid tiers. Read the tier, not the homepage."]}]
26:["$","h2","b4782",{"id":"the-seven-compared","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["The seven compared"]}]
27:["$","p","b4784",{"children":["Scenes you can create asks whether you can get a mockup in a setting nobody has photographed, and whether your logo survives the trip. Brand system asks how much of a brand you can pin into the work, and whether it stays pinned: palette and type at minimum, at best the voice, photography rules and do-and-don't guidance an agent reads on every generation, and a point for whether that setup follows you to the next piece of work or has to be rebuilt. Team access is how many people can be in the work before it starts costing per head."]}]
28:["$","div","b4785",{"role":"region","aria-label":"Comparison table, scroll horizontally to see all columns","tabIndex":0,"data-lenis-prevent":true,"className":"my-10 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-orange","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left","children":["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","b4786",{"className":"bg-black/[0.04]","children":[["$","td","b47860",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4789",{"children":[["$","strong","b4788",{"children":["Tool"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b47861",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4792",{"children":[["$","strong","b4791",{"children":["Mechanism"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b47862",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4795",{"children":[["$","strong","b4794",{"children":["Scenes you can create"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b47863",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4798",{"children":[["$","strong","b4797",{"children":["Brand system"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b47864",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4801",{"children":[["$","strong","b4800",{"children":["Team access"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b4802",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b48020",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4805",{"children":["Melius"]}]]}],["$","td","b48021",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4808",{"children":["Generative scene, composited artwork"]}]]}],["$","td","b48022",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4811",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b48023",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4814",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b48024",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4817",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b4818",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b48180",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4821",{"children":["Placeit"]}]]}],["$","td","b48181",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4824",{"children":["Template library"]}]]}],["$","td","b48182",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4827",{"children":["2/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b48183",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4830",{"children":["3/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b48184",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4833",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b4834",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b48340",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4837",{"children":["Illustrator Mockup"]}]]}],["$","td","b48341",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4840",{"children":["Inferred 3D, vector decal"]}]]}],["$","td","b48342",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4843",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b48343",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4846",{"children":["2/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b48344",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":"$L6e"}]]}],"$L6f","$L70","$L71","$L72"]}]}]}]
29:["$","h2","b4915",{"id":"1-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["1. Melius"]}]
2a:["$","p","b4917",{"children":["Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work. The canvas exists so an agent can assemble the pipeline and leave every step open to you. Describe the mockup in plain language and Mel, the Melius agent, builds the pipeline, choosing the right model for the scene and the right one for the type. The scene node and the logo node stay separate in the design process, which is the reason your logo survives properly in the final output. You're never forced to choose between a generated environment and an intact logo."]}]
2b:["$","p","b4925",{"children":["The Studio node is a layered editing surface with text overlays, and you can upload your own font file and use it in the layer panel. That means the practical workflow is: generate the scene, then composite the real logo as a layer on top, in your real typeface. Inpaint handles the middle ground by masking a region and regenerating only inside it, so a surface can be changed around artwork that stays put. Where a mark does have to be rendered into the image, per-step routing lets you send that node to GPT Image 2, which Melius recommends for visible typography and packaging shots with legible labels, while the surrounding scene goes to a model chosen for materials and lighting. The same node-separation logic carries over to ",["$","$L73","b4920",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b4919","href":"/blog/best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts","isNewTab":false},"children":["AI generated design concepts"]}]," and to ",["$","$L73","b4923",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b4922","href":"/blog/best-ai-tools-product-photo-variants","isNewTab":false},"children":["product photo variants"]}],"."]}]
2c:["$","p","b4927",{"children":["The brand system is a documented practice: a text node holding voice, hex codes, typography and photography rules, wired into every generation node on the canvas. It's reusable within a canvas, and worth knowing that it doesn't follow you to a new one, since context lives at the canvas level."]}]
2d:["$","h3","b4929",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
2e:["$","ul","b4931-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4931",{"children":["Layered compositing, so the real mark sits on top of a generated scene, in a font file you uploaded."]}],["$","li","b4933",{"children":["Per-step model routing, so the typography node and the material node can use different models."]}],["$","li","b4935",{"children":["Masked inpainting, which changes a surface without touching the artwork on it."]}],["$","li","b4937",{"children":["Real product details go in as context, which matters for packaging mockups."]}],["$","li","b4939",{"children":["Magic Resize re-composes a mockup per aspect ratio instead of cropping it."]}],["$","li","b4941",{"children":["Up to 8 seats on self-serve plans for your team and client reviewers, with unlimited seats on Enterprise."]}]]}]
2f:["$","p","b4943",{"children":["The trade-off: the fidelity here is a property of how you build the graph, not a guarantee the tool enforces. Ask a model to draw your logo and it will draw a logo. There's also no library of pre-shot scenes, so if what you want is a specific t-shirt on a specific model in three clicks, a template tool gets you there faster. And the brand anchor doesn't persist across canvases, which means copying it over or injecting it is a real step in the workflow."]}]
30:["$","p","b4951",{"children":["Paid plans start at an accessible monthly rate, with current pricing on the ",["$","$L73","b4946",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b4945","href":"/pricing","isNewTab":false},"children":["pricing page"]}]," and the current library of leading models on the ",["$","$L73","b4949",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b4948","href":"/models","isNewTab":false},"children":["models page"]}],"."]}]
31:["$","p","b4953",{"children":["Best for: brand and agency teams who need mockups in scenes nobody has photographed, and who need the logo in them to be the actual logo."]}]
32:["$","h2","b4955",{"id":"2-placeit","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["2. Placeit"]}]
33:["$","p","b4957",{"children":["Placeit is good at breadth, with a large mockup library and a template-library mechanism that preserves your artwork by construction. Upload the file, pick a scene, and the template conforms it to the fabric's folds and lighting, deterministically, every time."]}]
34:["$","p","b4959",{"children":["Its licensing is refreshingly plain: Placeit says a commercial license is included in all downloads, and the subscription carries unlimited downloads. The operative grant attaches to paid downloads, and it is revocable, so read the license terms if you are reselling."]}]
35:["$","h3","b4961",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
36:["$","ul","b4963-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4963",{"children":["A large scene library, spanning apparel, print, packaging and devices."]}],["$","li","b4965",{"children":["Fidelity here is structural: the template warps your exact file onto a pre-shot scene, so what comes back is the file you supplied."]}],["$","li","b4967",{"children":["A Brand Kit holding logo, palette and font pairing, applied from the editor and persisting across designs."]}],["$","li","b4969",{"children":["A commercial license on every paid download, and repeatable output, so the same scene gives the same result next quarter."]}]]}]
37:["$","p","b4971",{"children":["The trade-off: you're limited to scenes that already exist. If the brief calls for your packaging on a market stall in a specific light, no library has it, and this is where generative tools do their real work. Its Brand Kit stores your business name, logo, palette and font pairing and applies them from inside the editor, so the brand side is covered; it's the scenes that are fixed."]}]
38:["$","p","b4973",{"children":["Best for: standard mockups where a stock scene is fine and fidelity is non-negotiable."]}]
39:["$","h2","b4975",{"id":"3-adobe-illustrator-mockup","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["3. Adobe Illustrator Mockup"]}]
3a:["$","p","b4977",{"children":["Illustrator's Mockup feature shows that this job never required a generative model at all. A neural network predicts the shape of the scene from a single photograph, then meshing algorithms map a vector decal onto that inferred geometry. Adobe says the feature preserves the quality of a decal as users place it on the 3D surface, and it documents the mechanism, whereas the other vendors here only assert it."]}]
3b:["$","p","b4979",{"children":["For anyone already working in vector, the path from artwork to mockup is short: the logo is already in the file."]}]
3c:["$","h3","b4981",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
3d:["$","ul","b4983-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4983",{"children":["Vector decals stay vector, so the mark is resolution independent."]}],["$","li","b4985",{"children":["Works from a single ordinary photograph, with no prepared template needed."]}],["$","li","b4987",{"children":["Bundled with Illustrator, so it isn't another subscription."]}],["$","li","b4989",{"children":["Cylinders and simple curved surfaces such as mugs and cans map convincingly."]}]]}]
3e:["$","p","b4991",{"children":["The trade-off: the limits worth knowing are geometric. Testing the 2023 beta, CreativePro reported spheres came out poorly with no true spherical distortion, and fabric creases on a t-shirt were not followed, because the feature reads shape and not shading. Reviewers also reported the mapped artwork was not live-editable afterward, since expanding the appearance doesn't release the distorted logo. Mockup left beta in October 2024 and Adobe's release notes for that version claim precise vector placement on planar surfaces, which is exactly the flat-perspective case the beta handled worst, so treat the curved-surface findings as the ones still worth testing and re-test anything load-bearing on your own artwork. The feature requires Illustrator and the skills that go with it."]}]
3f:["$","p","b4993",{"children":["Best for: designers already in Illustrator putting vector marks onto simple curved surfaces."]}]
40:["$","h2","b4995",{"id":"4-pacdora","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["4. Pacdora"]}]
41:["$","p","b4997",{"children":["Pacdora is good at packaging specifically, and it's the only tool here that treats a dieline as a first-class object. It pairs a large mockup and dieline library with a real 3D render engine, so a box is an actual box with actual geometry rather than a photograph of one."]}]
42:["$","p","b4999",{"children":["For structural packaging work where the folds have to be right, that is the difference between a render and a proof."]}]
43:["$","h3","b5001",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
44:["$","ul","b5003-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b5003",{"children":["True 3D rendering, so artwork is a texture on real geometry and survives intact."]}],["$","li","b5005",{"children":["Dieline generation alongside the mockups."]}],["$","li","b5007",{"children":["High-resolution export on its higher tiers, plus video output, though the free tier exports no rendered images at all."]}],["$","li","b5009",{"children":["Free tier available for evaluation, with watermarked previews rather than exports."]}]]}]
45:["$","p","b5011",{"children":["The trade-off: the licensing needs reading carefully, because the split is sharp. Its lower tier is marked for personal use only, and commercial use plus a resale license arrive together only on its top tier. Pricing is per seat, billed annually or month-to-month, with the commercial tier costing meaningfully more."]}]
46:["$","p","b5013",{"children":["Best for: packaging design where structure and dielines matter as much as the render."]}]
47:["$","h2","b5015",{"id":"5-dynamic-mockups","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["5. Dynamic Mockups"]}]
48:["$","p","b5017",{"children":["Dynamic Mockups exists for volume and automation. Alongside its template library it exposes an application programming interface (API) and batch export, with product catalogs and saved templates, which makes it the natural fit for print-on-demand work where hundreds of designs go onto the same set of blanks."]}]
49:["$","p","b5019",{"children":["Its free tier gives watermark-free web exports, which is unusual here."]}]
4a:["$","h3","b5021",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
4b:["$","ul","b5023-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b5023",{"children":["An API and batch export, so mockups can be generated programmatically per stock keeping unit (SKU)."]}],["$","li","b5025",{"children":["Product catalogs and saved templates for repeatable output."]}],["$","li","b5027",{"children":["Unlimited saved templates once you're on the paid tier."]}],["$","li","b5029",{"children":["A free tier with watermark-free web exports."]}]]}]
4c:["$","p","b5031",{"children":["The trade-off: it ships both a library path and a generative path under one brand, and only the library path preserves your file, so it's on you to know which one you are using. API exports carry a watermark until you upgrade, while web exports don't. Worth reading the terms before you rely on it commercially, since the pricing page never mentions commercial use, and the terms of service license content for personal or internal business use only."]}]
4d:["$","p","b5033",{"children":["Best for: print-on-demand and catalog automation at volume."]}]
4e:["$","h2","b5035",{"id":"6-canva","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["6. Canva"]}]
4f:["$","p","b5037",{"children":["Canva covers the brand-system half of this, and its Brand Kit is deep. It acquired Smartmockups in 2021 and absorbed the library when the standalone site closed in 2024, so the scene collection is large, and the mockup templates preserve uploaded artwork."]}]
50:["$","p","b5039",{"children":["For a team already designing in Canva, the mockup is one step inside the document they are already building."]}]
51:["$","h3","b5041",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
52:["$","ul","b5043-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b5043",{"children":["A real brand kit applying fonts, colors and logos consistently across everything."]}],["$","li","b5045",{"children":["A large inherited mockup library from the Smartmockups acquisition."]}],["$","li","b5047",{"children":["Mockups sit inside the same document as the rest of the campaign."]}],["$","li","b5049",{"children":["A free tier that keeps the core tools."]}]]}]
53:["$","p","b5051",{"children":["The trade-off: Business is priced per person annually, so a reviewing stakeholder is a line item. Its generative tools sit alongside the template mockups, and the two behave differently on fidelity. Anyone still looking for smartmockups.com should know it closed on September 27, 2024 and now redirects to Canva's mockups page."]}]
54:["$","p","b5053",{"children":["Best for: teams already standardized on Canva who want brand consistency more than scene novelty."]}]
55:["$","h2","b5055",{"id":"7-recraft","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["7. Recraft"]}]
56:["$","p","b5057",{"children":["Recraft does the one thing that makes generated type recoverable: it outputs SVG, so lettering that comes back slightly wrong arrives as clean vector paths you can reshape in a design tool instead of regenerating the whole image. In a category where typography is the main failure mode, that means a wrong letter is fixable."]}]
57:["$","p","b5059",{"children":["It also handles 300 DPI and CMYK output, which matters if the mockup is heading toward print."]}]
58:["$","h3","b5061",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
59:["$","ul","b5063-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b5063",{"children":["Native SVG output with clean paths and structured layers, so lettering can be reshaped by hand."]}],["$","li","b5065",{"children":["300 DPI and CMYK support for print-bound work."]}],["$","li","b5067",{"children":["Both a template path and a generative path, covering two mechanisms in one tool."]}],["$","li","b5069",{"children":["A free tier of daily generations for evaluation."]}]]}]
5a:["$","p","b5071",{"children":["The trade-off: the free plan is the one to read closely. Images generated on it are owned by Recraft, appear publicly in its community gallery, and carry no commercial license. Ownership and commercial rights arrive on the paid tiers, and Recraft's terms say images made while subscribed stay yours after the subscription ends. Two things to set expectations on: generated text arrives as outlined paths, so you can reshape a letter but you cannot retype a word, and its chat mode, which Recraft calls Agentic, carries context between turns and will chain a few steps, though it is not building a graph you keep."]}]
5b:["$","p","b5073",{"children":["Best for: work where generated type has to be fixable, and print output is the destination."]}]
5c:["$","h2","b5075",{"id":"when-a-template-beats-a-generated-mockup","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["When a template beats a generated mockup"]}]
5d:["$","p","b5077",{"children":["If the scene you need already exists, use the template. A t-shirt on a plain background, a phone in a hand, a poster on a brick wall: these are solved and free of fidelity risk, and generating them is slower. The library tools in this comparison exist because most mockup requests are ordinary."]}]
5e:["$","p","b5079",{"children":["Generation pays off when the scene doesn't exist and can't be shot: your packaging in a market you have never photographed, or a summer product in February. At that point the question stops being which tool has more templates and becomes whether the workflow can put your real artwork into an invented world without redrawing it. That's a compositing problem. The tools that keep the scene and the logo as separate steps can take that brief; the library tools can't."]}]
5f:["$","h2","b5081",{"id":"frequently-asked-questions","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Frequently asked questions"]}]
60:["$","div","b5082",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the best AI tool for brand mockups?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"The best AI brand mockup tool depends on whether the scene you need already exists. If it doesn't, a canvas that generates the scene and composites your real logo on top, such as Melius, gets you a mockup nobody has photographed without redrawing your logo, and keeps the graph so the next brief starts from it. If the scene does already exist, a template-library tool like Placeit is quick and preserves your file by construction. For packaging with real structure, Pacdora's 3D renderer and dielines do a job the template tools don't attempt."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Will AI mockup tools distort my logo?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Generative mockup tools will distort a logo unless the workflow puts your logo back on top as a layer. A diffusion model redraws the whole frame, so your mark is re-synthesized from scratch, which shows up as tapered strokes, shifted corner radii and garbled small text. Template libraries and 3D renderers don't have this problem at all, because your file is warped or mapped onto the surface. On a generative canvas the fix is compositing the real asset as a layer, or masking the region so only the surroundings regenerate."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Which AI model is best at text in images?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"GPT Image 2 is the model most often cited for multilingual in-image text, and OpenAI's own launch material names Bengali, Chinese, Hindi, Japanese and Korean as the languages where it gained most. Ideogram 4.0 takes bounding boxes and hex colors as structured input for layout, and Recraft's SVG output gives you letterforms as vector paths you can reshape by hand. Reliability falls away as the text gets longer on all of them, and Ideogram's own guide says long passages belong in a graphic editor afterward, so packaging back panels remain out of reach."}]]}],"$L74","$L75","$L76"]}]
61:["$","p","b5087",{"children":["Generate the scene nobody has photographed, then composite your real logo on top in your real typeface, in one graph you can re-run for the next brief. ",["$","$L73","b5085",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b5084","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true},"children":["Open Melius"]}],"."]}]
62:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L77","post-best-ai-tools-jewelry-product-photos",{"post":{"_key":"post-best-ai-tools-jewelry-product-photos","slug":"best-ai-tools-jewelry-product-photos","category":"comparisons","title":"Best AI tools for jewelry product photos","isoDate":"2026-09-09","date":"September 9, 2026","readTime":"11 Min Read","excerpt":"Seven AI tools compared for jewelry photography, judged on whether your actual piece survives the edit, plus on-model shots, scale, and metal and stone fidelity.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/best-ai-tools-jewelry-product-photos/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Melius Team"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the best AI tool for jewelry product photography?","answer":"The best AI tool for jewelry product photography depends on whether you need the background changed or the piece worn. For background and scene work where the item must not change, tools with an explicit position-locking mode, like Claid's Precise mode, do that job directly. For on-model shots and catalog workflows, a canvas that lets you supply real product data and composite the actual asset, like Melius, keeps fidelity under your control. Tools with a dedicated jewelry studio, such as Photta, are worth testing on your hardest piece."},{"question":"Why do general AI photo tools struggle with jewelry?","answer":"General AI photo tools struggle with jewelry because they were trained largely on apparel, and jewelry geometry is unfamiliar to those priors. Faced with a complicated setting, the model resolves it toward what a ring or a necklace usually looks like: prong counts change, claw settings read as bezel, stone placement drifts, and fine chains blur. The output looks like jewelry, it just isn't your jewelry, and that's a returns problem as much as an aesthetic one."},{"question":"Can AI generate on-model jewelry photos of rings and necklaces?","answer":"Yes, AI can generate on-model jewelry photos of rings and necklaces, and it's the least reliable thing in the category. Pixelcut names a jewelry format for pieces worn on a wrist, neck or ear, Flair and Photta both generate worn shots, and Melius generates them on the canvas from your own reference. Claid publishes the specific limitation worth knowing: the models don't yet reliably understand how clasps and ear wires work, so asymmetrical pieces and complicated fastenings are where worn shots fail first."},{"question":"Can AI handle reflections in gold and silver jewelry?","answer":"AI handles reflections in gold and silver only partially, and it is the hardest optical problem in the category. Polished metal behaves like a mirror and reflects the whole room, which is why studio photographers cross-polarize their lights at the point of capture. Pixelcut claims specifically to render highlights and mirror-like reflections cleanly, and Claid's Precise mode keeps the original reflections intact by not regenerating the product at all. Watch the color too: oversaturated gold reads orange and oversaturated silver goes blue, and both cost trust."},{"question":"Can I use AI jewelry photos on Amazon, Etsy and Shopify?","answer":"Yes, subject to each marketplace's image rules and to the images being accurate. Amazon requires the main image to sit on a pure white background with the product filling 85% or more of the frame, which is what a background-removal step producing a transparent or white field is for. The rule governs the main image; the rest of the gallery can use other backgrounds. It's accuracy that constrains you here, not policy: if the generated image shows a different stone count or setting than the piece you ship, that is a returns and trust problem regardless of what the platform allows."},{"question":"How do you keep jewelry photos consistent across a whole catalog?","answer":"Consistency across a catalog comes from building the look once as a re-runnable workflow you point at each new piece. On a node canvas that means a graph holding your lighting direction, background treatment and framing, pointed at a new product each time, so SKU 200 matches SKU 1. Tools offering custom model training, like Flair, get at the same goal differently by teaching a model your house style. Editing images one at a time is what stops scaling at roughly the fiftieth piece."},{"question":"Do I still need a photographer?","answer":"You still need a photographer for hero images on high-value pieces. Cross-polarized lighting and focus stacking on a macro lens still beat generated output where the image carries the sale. Generated images cover the long tail well: variants, seasonal backgrounds, channel resizes and the SKUs nobody was going to book studio time for. Generation also can't rescue a bad input: a soft or fingerprinted photograph gives the model nothing accurate to preserve."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"what-is-the-best-ai-tool-for-jewelry-product-photos","title":"What is the best AI tool for jewelry product photos?"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"What to know before you pick"},{"_key":"why-jewelry-is-the-hardest-product-category-to-shoot","title":"Why jewelry is the hardest product category to shoot"},{"_key":"what-separates-a-good-ai-jewelry-tool","title":"What separates a good AI jewelry tool"},{"_key":"the-seven-compared","title":"The seven compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-claid","title":"2. Claid"},{"_key":"3-pixelcut","title":"3. Pixelcut"},{"_key":"4-photta","title":"4. Photta"},{"_key":"5-flair","title":"5. Flair"},{"_key":"6-photoroom","title":"6. Photoroom"},{"_key":"7-comfyui","title":"7. ComfyUI"},{"_key":"when-ai-is-the-wrong-choice-for-a-piece","title":"When AI is the wrong choice for a piece"},{"_key":"building-a-jewelry-workflow-on-melius","title":"Building a jewelry workflow on Melius"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"Frequently asked questions"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4369","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4368","text":"What is the best AI tool for jewelry product photos?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-is-the-best-ai-tool-for-jewelry-product-photos"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4371","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4370","text":"The best AI tool for jewelry product photos is the one that gives you back the exact piece you uploaded, prong count and all, instead of a plausible ring that resembles it. That sounds obvious and it's the single thing most of this category gets wrong: a model trained mostly on apparel meets a scattered-baguette ring, falls back on what a ring usually looks like, and hands you something that reads as jewelry but is not the item in your inventory. A shirt collar rendered a little differently is still the shirt. A ring with its prong count changed is a different product.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4373","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4372","text":"So the useful question isn't which tool makes the prettiest image. It's which tool holds geometry, metal and stone detail while it changes everything around them. On that test the category splits in two: general-purpose product photography tools that sell you a scene, and jewelry-first tools that sell you geometry preservation.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4375","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4374","text":"What to know before you pick","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-pick"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4377","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4376","text":"Ask what the tool does to your piece. Background handling is the easy half: a swap around a cut-out preserves the product by construction, while a full regeneration redraws it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4379","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4378","text":"On-model is where fidelity breaks first. Clasps, ear wires and asymmetrical pieces are the specific failure cases.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4381","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4380","text":"Scale decides conversions. Baymard Institute found 42% of test participants try to gauge a product's size from its images, and a ring photographed alone gives them nothing to judge against.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4383","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4382","text":"Over-retouching costs money later. If the piece looks better than the real thing, the gap comes back as a return.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4385","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4384","text":"Why jewelry is the hardest product category to shoot","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-jewelry-is-the-hardest-product-category-to-shoot"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4387","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4386","text":"Understanding what a human photographer struggles with explains what the models struggle with, because they are the same four problems.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4389","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4388","text":"Depth of field collapses at macro distances, often to under a millimeter at 1:1 magnification, which is why focus stacking is standard practice. Polished metal behaves like a mirror, so professionals cross-polarize, putting a filter on each light and another on the lens turned 90 degrees to them. Color is unstable across gold, rose gold and silver, which is why studios shoot a color reference at the top of every session and hold every lamp at the same temperature. And gemstones refract rather than simply reflect, so sparkle has to read as natural instead of blown out.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4391","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4390","text":"A generative model doesn't have any of that apparatus. It has priors. When those priors were built mostly on clothing, the model resolves an unfamiliar setting into a familiar one: claw-set reads as bezel-set, stone counts drift, fine chains blur, a domed band flattens. In March 2026 FormaNova, which sells a jewelry photography tool, put a single wide brushed-gold ring with scattered baguettes through five tools at default settings and reported that one simplified the band to a plain one, another reinterpreted the setting as channel-set, a third turned it into stacked bands, and a fourth returned something unrecognizable. The fifth was FormaNova's own tool, which preserved it. Read that ranking as marketing: the vendor graded its own exam, on one ring, three days before publishing. The failure taxonomy is worth more than the ranking, because it names specific things you can reproduce on your own hardest piece in an afternoon, which is the only test that settles it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4393","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4392","text":"What separates a good AI jewelry tool","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-separates-a-good-ai-jewelry-tool"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4395","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4394","text":"There are four criteria, and the first decides whether the output is usable at all.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4397","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4396","text":"Whether your piece survives","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4399","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4398","text":"Look for a stated mechanism, not a promise of quality. Locking the product's position and angle while only the background changes is a mechanism. Masking a region and regenerating only outside it is a mechanism. Feeding the model real dimensions and materials, so it is not inferring them from one photograph, is a mechanism. \"Trained for jewelry\" is a claim.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4401","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4400","text":"Whether it can put the piece on a person","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4403","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4402","text":"On-model shots solve scale, and scale is worth real money. Baymard's testing found that 42% of participants try to gauge size from product images, and that when they cannot, they draw inaccurate conclusions, discarding relevant products and in some cases abandoning the site. That's what a hand, a neck or an ear is for: the size reference. It's also the hardest thing to generate, because the model has to get both the jewelry and the anatomy right, and the join between them.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4405","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4404","text":"Whether it holds a look across a catalog","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4407","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4406","text":"One good image is a demo. A jewelry catalog is hundreds of stock keeping units (SKUs) that have to look like they belong to the same brand, shot the same way, across a marketplace listing, a product page and a paid social placement. That's a workflow question, and it's where single-image tools stop being useful.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4409","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4408","text":"What it costs to add a person who does not generate","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4411","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4410","text":"Jewelry work gets reviewed, by a merchandiser, a founder or a client. Most tools in this category throttle on seats, and the caps are low: several cap at one, two, five or fifteen people. Worth checking before the tool becomes the reason approvals happen over email attachments.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4413","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4412","text":"The seven compared","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-seven-compared"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4415","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4414","text":"Product fidelity counts the documented mechanisms a tool uses to keep your actual piece intact, out of five: real product details fed in as context, a reference wired into generation, masked regeneration, compositing your original asset, and a background step that preserves the cut-out. Catalog reuse asks whether one setup runs across hundreds of SKUs without being rebuilt. Team access is how many people can be in the work before it starts costing per head. Where a vendor publishes no seat data we say so instead of guessing.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b4416","rows":[{"_key":"b4417","cells":[{"_key":"b4418","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4420","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4419","text":"Tool","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b4421","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4423","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4422","text":"On-model jewelry","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b4424","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4426","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4425","text":"Product fidelity","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b4427","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4429","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4428","text":"Catalog reuse","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b4430","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4432","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4431","text":"Team access","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4433","cells":[{"_key":"b4434","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4436","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4435","text":"Melius","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4437","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4439","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4438","text":"Yes, with your own reference wired in","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4440","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4442","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4441","text":"5/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4443","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4445","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4444","text":"5/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4446","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4448","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4447","text":"5/5","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4449","cells":[{"_key":"b4450","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4452","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4451","text":"Claid","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4453","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4455","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4454","text":"Creative mode only, vendor-hedged","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4456","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4458","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4457","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4459","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4461","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4460","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4462","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4464","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4463","text":"Not disclosed","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4465","cells":[{"_key":"b4466","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4468","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4467","text":"Pixelcut","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4469","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4471","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4470","text":"Yes, named Jewelry Scene format","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4472","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4474","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4473","text":"2/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4475","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4477","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4476","text":"2/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4478","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4480","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4479","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4481","cells":[{"_key":"b4482","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4484","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4483","text":"Photta","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4485","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4487","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4486","text":"Yes, try-on and posed","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4488","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4490","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4489","text":"2/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4491","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4493","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4492","text":"2/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4494","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4496","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4495","text":"2/5","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4497","cells":[{"_key":"b4498","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4500","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4499","text":"Flair","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4501","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4503","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4502","text":"Yes, across model types","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4504","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4506","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4505","text":"1/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4507","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4509","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4508","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4510","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4512","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4511","text":"Not disclosed","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4513","cells":[{"_key":"b4514","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4516","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4515","text":"Photoroom","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4517","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4519","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4518","text":"Yes, via AI virtual models","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4520","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4522","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4521","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4523","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4525","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4524","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4526","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4528","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4527","text":"4/5","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4529","cells":[{"_key":"b4530","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4532","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4531","text":"ComfyUI","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4533","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4535","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4534","text":"Buildable, not provided","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4536","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4538","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4537","text":"4/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4539","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4541","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4540","text":"4/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4542","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4544","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4543","text":"1/5","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4546","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4545","text":"1. Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"1-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4548","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4547","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work. Tell it the shot you want, and the Melius agent Mel assembles the graph, picking a model per step. Every node it chooses stays editable, which for jewelry is the point: the reference wiring is where fidelity is won or lost, and that happens before anything is generated.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4550","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4549","text":"Two mechanisms do most of the work. The first is context: provide a product image, then add details like dimensions, materials, colors and product copy in a text node to improve the final outputs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4552","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4551","text":"The second is compositing. Melius's Studio node is a layered editing surface with text overlays and custom font support, so a scene can be generated while the real asset sits on top as a layer and is never redrawn. Paired with Melius tools like Inpaint, which masks a region and regenerates only inside of it, and Remove Background, which outputs a transparent PNG for a marketplace listing that requires a pure white field, the workflow can change the world around a piece without asking a model to reinvent the piece.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4554","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4553","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4556","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4555","text":"Real product details go in as context, so the model works from actual dimensions and materials.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4558","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4557","text":"Per-step model routing, with the documentation recommending different models for material and skin tone than for legible type.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4560","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4559","text":"Layered compositing, masked inpainting and background removal, so the piece survives while the scene around it changes.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4562","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4561","text":"Upscaling from 1K to 2K or 4K, so macro detail survives a zoom.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4564","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4563","text":"Magic Resize re-composes for each channel's aspect ratio instead of cropping the piece out of frame.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4566","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4565","text":"Up to 8 seats on self-serve plans for your team and reviewers, with unlimited seats on Enterprise.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4568","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4567","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4570","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4569","text":"Melius is a general-purpose canvas, not a jewelry-trained system. A tool built only for jewelry has priors tuned to clasps and settings, and on a first pass with no reference wiring it may well read a complicated ring more accurately. The Melius answer is discipline: supply the real details, wire the reference, composite the asset. That works, and it asks more of you than pressing one button.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4572","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4571","text":"Best for: jewelry brands running a catalog who want one workflow they can re-run per SKU, and who care more about the piece being right than about the first click being fast.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4574","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4573","text":"2. Claid","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"2-claid"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4576","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4575","text":"Claid tells you where its own limits are. In this category that is worth more than it sounds. Its AI Photoshoot now runs five modes, and two of them carry the honest version of the fidelity question: Precise mode locks the jewelry in its original position and angle, keeping proportions and reflections intact while only the background changes, while Creative mode can alter perspective, lighting and angle, and is where on-model output comes from.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4578","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4577","text":"It also publishes a specific limitation no other vendor here matches, warning that AI is not yet smart enough to understand complex jewelry, especially how different clasps or earwires work, and recommending flat lays over on-model for asymmetrical pieces.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4580","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4579","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4582","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4581","text":"A documented fidelity mechanism, stated as a guarantee rather than a claim.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4584","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4583","text":"A published, specific account of which jewelry types it handles poorly.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4586","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4585","text":"Background removal, upscaling, video and an application programming interface (API) alongside the photoshoot tools.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4588","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4587","text":"A free trial of 50 credits, with AI Photoshoot at 4 credits per generation at standard quality and 10 at studio.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4590","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4589","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4592","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4591","text":"The fidelity guarantee only holds in Precise mode, and Precise mode can't put a piece on a person, so the two things you most want are on opposite sides of a switch. Seat structure is not disclosed on the pricing page.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4594","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4593","text":"Best for: catalog work where the background changes and the piece must not.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4596","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4595","text":"3. Pixelcut","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"3-pixelcut"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4598","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4597","text":"Pixelcut's jewelry claim is specific enough to check. It names a Jewelry Scene format for pieces worn on a wrist, neck or ear, and states that the shape, engraving, stone setting and clasp of the uploaded item are kept, with hallmarks and fine text staying crisp.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4600","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4599","text":"It also addresses the reflection problem directly, describing how polished gold, silver and faceted stones bounce light in ways that are hard to control, and claiming to render those highlights and mirror-like reflections cleanly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4602","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4601","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4604","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4603","text":"A named on-model jewelry format, built for the category.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4606","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4605","text":"An explicit, itemized fidelity claim covering engraving, setting and clasp.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4608","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4607","text":"Mobile-first, for a founder photographing stock on a phone.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4610","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4609","text":"Seats come included, not billed per head: 3 on Pro, 10 or more on Business.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4612","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4611","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4614","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4613","text":"The fidelity claims are the vendor's own and carry no published mechanism or third-party test behind them, so they are worth verifying against your own hardest piece before committing a catalog. Its own FAQ also lists a shorter version of the guarantee than its body copy does, swapping the clasp for the metal, which is a small thing to be inconsistent about in the one claim you are selling on.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4616","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4615","text":"Best for: small jewelry sellers who want on-model output from a phone without building a workflow.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4618","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4617","text":"4. Photta","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"4-photta"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4620","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4619","text":"Photta is a fashion and apparel tool with a dedicated Jewelry Studio alongside its apparel, eyewear and product studios, and it's transparent about unit economics. It publishes per-action credit costs: 5 credits for a try-on, 4 for an AI model, 3 for a new pose, 1 for an upscale, 1 for a background.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4622","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4621","text":"For a seller who wants to know what a hundred product shots will actually cost before signing up, that openness is useful and rare in this category.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4624","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4623","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4626","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4625","text":"A studio built specifically for jewelry.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4628","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4627","text":"Per-action credit pricing published openly, so cost per SKU is calculable in advance.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4630","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4629","text":"Tiers scale by photo volume, from 30 photos a month to 1,000.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4632","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4631","text":"Try-on and pose generation as first-class actions.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4634","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4633","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4636","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4635","text":"Seats are the throttle and the caps are explicit: one, two, five and fifteen across the four tiers, so collaboration is a pricing decision. There's no free plan, only a 20-credit trial that needs no card, and its published case-study conversion figure is self-reported on a single customer.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4638","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4637","text":"Best for: sellers who want a category-specific studio and can work within a seat cap.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4640","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4639","text":"5. Flair","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"5-flair"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4642","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4641","text":"Flair is good at scene staging, with a drag-and-drop surface for arranging a product in a set, and it states that its models are trained to render fine jewelry detail including gemstone cuts, metal finishes and fine design detail. On-model output spans a range of skin tones, ages and styles.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4644","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4643","text":"It supports custom trained models, which is the route to a consistent house look across a catalog.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4646","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4645","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4648","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4647","text":"An explicit fine-jewelry training claim covering gemstone cuts and metal finishes.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4650","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4649","text":"Custom model training for a repeatable brand look.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4652","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4651","text":"A usable free tier with one custom model and five images.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4654","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4653","text":"Low entry pricing, with a paid tier from $8 a month.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4656","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4655","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4658","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4657","text":"Its own editing toolbar includes a Regenerate Product action, which is a fair signal that the product is regenerated rather than preserved, so this sits on the generative side of the fidelity line. A company commercial license first appears on the $26 tier, not the $8 one, which is worth knowing before publishing output.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4660","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4659","text":"Best for: staged scene work where the setting matters more than millimeter-accurate geometry.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4662","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4661","text":"6. Photoroom","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"6-photoroom"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4664","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4663","text":"Photoroom is good at the background half of the job and has deep tooling for it: background removal, AI backgrounds, AI shadows, a Product Beautifier and a Fix Product brush, plus video. For cut-out and re-staging work at volume it's a mature, fast option.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4666","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4665","text":"It also generates worn jewelry through its AI virtual models, and its seat allowance is generous for a general-purpose tool, at up to 50 across paid tiers.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4668","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4667","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4670","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4669","text":"Strong, well-established cut-out and background replacement.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4672","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4671","text":"AI shadows, the detail that usually gives a composite away.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4674","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4673","text":"Up to 50 seats on paid tiers, which is high for this category.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4676","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4675","text":"Worn-jewelry generation via AI virtual models, though Photoroom's own jewelry page describes them as scene placement, not on-body wear.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4678","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4677","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4680","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4679","text":"The fidelity story is the weak part: it's a cut-out and background tool at heart, with generative virtual models layered on, and no stated mechanism for holding a setting or a stone count. Its jewelry performance figures are vendor-published with no methodology, and its two jewelry pages carry entirely different stat sets: one claims 2x sales growth, the other +23% conversion. A third asset, a survey of a thousand-plus jewelry brands, is the only one that states a method, and its cost-reduction figure of 93% does not match the 89% on the industry page.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4682","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4681","text":"Best for: high-volume background and scene work, with worn shots available when a cut-out is not enough.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4684","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4683","text":"7. ComfyUI","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"7-comfyui"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4686","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4685","text":"ComfyUI is free, open source, and the option here where you control the fidelity mechanism yourself. Masked inpainting plus an explicit composite-back step lets you build a pipeline that changes a background and returns the product pixel-identical. The composite matters: the standard latent inpainting path decodes the whole frame, so unmasked areas shift measurably unless you paste the original back through the mask. That is the guarantee the commercial tools are approximating, and it holds only if you build it correctly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4688","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4687","text":"For a technical operator with a catalog large enough to justify the setup, that control is real.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4690","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4689","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4692","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4691","text":"Complete control over masking and compositing, so product preservation is something you can guarantee rather than trust.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4694","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4693","text":"Free and self-hosted, with no per-image billing on your own hardware.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4696","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4695","text":"Any model you can install locally, including ones no commercial platform offers, though ControlNet preprocessors and IPAdapter are community add-ons rather than core.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4698","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4697","text":"A deep ecosystem of community workflows for product photography.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4700","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4699","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4702","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4701","text":"Nothing is provided, everything is assembled, and you become responsible for models, dependencies and a graphics processing unit (GPU). There's no on-model jewelry capability out of the box and collaboration is close to absent.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4704","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4703","text":"Best for: technical operators who want a guarantee they built themselves, and have time to build it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4706","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4705","text":"When AI is the wrong choice for a piece","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"when-ai-is-the-wrong-choice-for-a-piece"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4708","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4707","text":"For a hero image on a high-value piece, hire a photographer. A one-carat solitaire on a landing page justifies cross-polarized lighting and focus stacking, and no current model beats that. Generated imagery pays off on the long tail: the hundredth SKU, the seasonal background, the channel resize, the variant nobody was going to book studio time for.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4710","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4709","text":"There's also a floor no tool clears. If the input photograph is soft, badly lit or covered in fingerprints, the model has nothing accurate to preserve, and preservation is the whole argument. Clean the piece, shoot it sharp, then let the workflow handle everything that comes after.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4712","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4711","text":"Building a jewelry workflow on Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"building-a-jewelry-workflow-on-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4717","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b4714","href":"/blog/best-ai-tools-product-photo-variants","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4713","text":"Start with one sharp product photo and a text node carrying the details that matter: dimensions, metal, stone type, setting style. The agent routes each step to the right model, and the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4715","text":"product variant workflow","marks":["b4714"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4716","text":" applies the same way it does to any other product category, except that the composite step is non-negotiable for jewelry.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4722","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b4719","href":"/blog/best-ai-photo-background-editing-tools","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4718","text":"Use Remove Background for marketplace listings that require a white field, Inpaint to change the scene without touching the piece, and Studio to layer the real asset over a generated background. Magic Resize re-composes for each channel's ratio instead of cropping, which matters when the piece is small and a crop loses it. The same ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4720","text":"background editing workflow","marks":["b4719"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4721","text":" covers the background side in detail.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4724","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4723","text":"The honest limit is the first pass on a piece with an unusual setting. A jewelry-specific tool's priors will read it more accurately without help. The Melius answer is to supply the help: real dimensions, real materials, a wired reference. That closes the gap, and it scales to the next hundred SKUs in a way that pressing one button a hundred times does not.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4726","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4725","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b4727","items":"$62:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4732","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b4729","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4728","text":"Give an agent your product image and the details that matter, and build one jewelry workflow you can re-run for every piece. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4730","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b4729"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4731","text":".","marks":[]}]}]}}],"$L78","$L79"]}]]}]]}]
